Input: {"question": "What is the format of \"Swan Princess\"?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d00", "start": 0, "end": 85, "text": "by seven direct-to-video sequels and is the only film of the series to be theatrical."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d00", "start": 86, "end": 176, "text": "The theme song \"Far Longer than Forever\" is performed by Regina Belle and Jeffrey Osborne."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d00", "start": 177, "end": 250, "text": "The song was nominated for a Golden Globe in 1995 for Best Original Song."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d00", "start": 251, "end": 427, "text": "The evil sorcerer Rothbart (Jack Palance) is planning to take King William's (Dakin Matthews) kingdom for himself by mastering a type of dark magic known as The Forbidden Arts."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d00", "start": 428, "end": 471, "text": "Before he can strike, Rothbart is arrested."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d00", "start": 472, "end": 554, "text": "Despite calls for his death, King William spares Rothbart's life and banishes him."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d00", "start": 555, "end": 596, "text": "A hateful Rothbart swears to King William"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d01", "start": 0, "end": 67, "text": "on November 18, 1994, where it received mixed reviews from critics."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d01", "start": 68, "end": 159, "text": "The Swan Princess: Music from the Motion Picture is the soundtrack album of the first film."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d01", "start": 160, "end": 309, "text": "\"Far Longer than Forever\" is the theme song for the first film \"The Swan Princess\" and was nominated for a Golden Globe Award for Best Original Song."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d01", "start": 310, "end": 362, "text": "It is performed by Regina Belle and Jeffrey Osborne."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d01", "start": 363, "end": 577, "text": "The Swan Princess: Escape from Castle Mountain / The Swan Princess: The Secret of the Castle is a 1997 American animated musical-fantasy film and the direct-to-video sequel to the animated film \"The Swan Princess\"."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d01", "start": 578, "end": 597, "text": "Directed by Richard"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d02", "start": 0, "end": 21, "text": "in the previous year."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d02", "start": 22, "end": 139, "text": "Ridden by the Welsh jockey Taffy Thomas she went to the front as usual and opened up a clear lead over her opponents."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d02", "start": 140, "end": 291, "text": "She was strongly pressed in the closing stages by the favourite Band Practice (a colt from the Dermot Weld stable) but stayed on well to win by a head."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d02", "start": 292, "end": 432, "text": "Later that month she was matched against older horses in William Hill Sprint Championship at York in which she finished sixth behind Sharpo."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d02", "start": 433, "end": 539, "text": "At the end of the year Swan Princess was rated the best two-year-old filly to race in Ireland on the Irish"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0441-ee600b8ae73b:d03", "start": 0, "end": 594, "text": "The Swan Princess ( film series ) - Wikipedia Jump to content 